      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "The gelid river by the Reedy Bank"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A river crab large enough to clamber into the punt."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Special defenses mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Magic resistance · 25% magic resistance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Sticking oars at M · When rowing upstream, the oars stick after three attempts. While an oar is stuck, there is a 1-in-6 chance each round that a giant crab climbs into the boat and attacks. Free the oar using the procedure for opening a door. The crabs walk on the gelid surface and leave the punt upright here.",
            "Reedy Bank at N · If the party tries to continue downstream from N, a giant crab upsets or holes the boat before they get started. Upstream from N is possible only if they arrived from area O. That route toward M uses the sticking-oar and crab encounter rules."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "The punting encounter supplies the 24 HP value.",
            "Gary Gygax, The Land Beyond the Magic Mirror (TSR, 1983), M. Large Punt and N. Reedy Bank, p. 19."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "portrait": {
        "url": "",
        "credit": "OpenAI ImageGen · The Lost Hope"
      }
    },
