        ]
      ],
      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Manor house banquet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A heavy-bodied ape that appears as a large monkey to guests under the banquet’s delusion."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Special attacks and defenses mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Rend · When both forelimb attacks hit, the ape deals an additional 1–8 rending damage.",
            "Magic resistance · 25% magic resistance."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Banquet ambush · Three apes with 25 HP each try to rise and attack alongside the giant wolverines when the banquet erupts into combat. The printed attack order places the apes after the wolverines and the next wave of 26 larvae crossing the table. Characters still wearing crowns of delusion misread the attacks as affection."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "Gary Gygax, The Land Beyond the Magic Mirror (TSR, 1983), The Mad Feast Hall, CA, pp. 24–25."
          ]
        }
      ],
