      "sections": [
        {
          "title": "Habitats",
          "lines": [
            "Manor house banquet"
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Appearance",
          "lines": [
            "A great shaggy wolverine that seems like a harmless teddy bear to guests under the banquet’s delusion."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Special attacks mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Ferocity · The wolverine gains +4 to hit.",
            "Musk · The wolverine can spray one target behind it. The target saves vs. Poison or is blinded for 1–8 hours. A successful save still causes 2–8 turns of nausea and cuts Strength and Dexterity by half for that duration. Worn cloth saves as if attacked by acid. On failure it rots and is destroyed."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Encounters mechanics",
          "lines": [
            "Banquet ambush · Two wolverines with 22 HP each try to rise and attack alongside the carnivorous apes when the banquet erupts into combat. The printed attack order places the wolverines before the next wave of 26 larvae crossing the table, followed by the apes."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Table notes",
          "lines": [
            "The encounter block gives no magic resistance. The Afterword on p. 26 separately discusses 25% magic resistance for creatures native to the land or long accustomed to it.",
            "Gary Gygax, The Land Beyond the Magic Mirror (TSR, 1983), The Mad Feast Hall, GW, pp. 24–25."
          ]
        }
      ],
